        "evidence": "Part 1 - What happened: E2E Driver used frequent formative checks (counting parts, asking students to name numerator/denominator, asking which of two fractions is a proper fraction) that aligned with the stated learning focus. These checks assessed recall and basic understanding (identifying parts and labels) more than higher-order reasoning. A short independent task (write proper fractions for given shapes) was assigned at the end, but there was no evidence of follow-up marking or targeted remediation during the lesson.\nPart 2 - Quote: \"If I say 3/7 or 7/3 which one is a proper fraction?\" \"Which one is a proper fraction — 3/7?\"",
